### Frequency Barcharts / Barplots

::: {.callout-warning appearance=simple}

Another common way to display categorical data frequencies is a barchart/barplot.
:::  

A Barchart or barplot takes these frequencies, and draws bars along the X-axis where the height of the bars is determined by the frequencies seen in the table. 

::: {.panel-tabset}

## base

To create a barplot/barchart in base graphics requires the data to be in summarized in a table form first. Then the result of the table is plotted. The first argument is the table to be plotted, the `main` argument controls the title. 

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ps <- table(pen$species)
barplot(ps, main="Frequency of Penguins by Species")
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](data_viz_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-8-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


::: {.callout-warning appearance=simple}

> note yaxis direction and no labels at top of bar

:::  


## ggplot
The geometry needed to draw a barchart in ggplot is `geom_bar()`.

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(pen, aes(x=species)) + geom_bar()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](data_viz_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-9-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


**Adding Annotation**

The biggest addition to increase the readability of a barchart is to add the frequencies on top of the bars. 


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(pen, aes(x=species)) + theme_bw() + 
    geom_bar(aes(y = ..count..)) + ggtitle("Frequency of penguins by species") + 
    geom_text(aes(y=..count.. + 10, label=..count..), stat='count', size = 5)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](data_viz_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-10-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::



## sjPlot
::: {.callout-warning appearance=simple}

The [sjPlot](https://strengejacke.github.io/sjPlot/) package will automatically add frequencies for you, making it the preferred package for these situations.

:::  


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot_frq(pen, species,
         title = "Count of penguins by species")
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](data_viz_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-11-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::



